00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.909 align:start position:0%
the new beyond light expansion provides  more of what destiny 2 is good at  satisfying first-person shooting  fascinating places to explore  a whole lot of pungy guns to try out and  a great inventive raid  it also maintains some of the game's  lingering problems though like a  reliance on repetitive content and  time-sucking grinds to arbitrarily raise  numbers  to put it simply beyond light is largely  more destiny  if that's a thing you like you'll enjoy  it and if it's a thing you complain  about you probably won't  the last two years have seen bungie  making changes to destiny 2  both large and incremental that are  improving the game deepening its world  and expanding its experiences  beyond light is perhaps the best told  story that developer bungie has put  forth in the game  the focus is on characters who have  feelings and motivations which allows  them to grow beyond being just voices on  the radio  yelling at you to go shoot another world  threatening alien  and new additions to the game like a  host of freezing abilities called stasis  change up the gameplay and combat  strategies in fun and unexpected ways  the new expansion takes you to europa  one of jupiter's frozen moons to uncover  secrets about the latest threat invading  the solar system  the darkness for the last few seasons of  destiny 2  we've been puzzling out what the  darkness has in store for us but instead  of attacking  the darkness is offering seductive power  it doesn't want to kill the guardian  heroes that players control  it wants to own them  you answered we've kept you waiting long  enough  come to us salvation awaits  much of the story of beyond light is  about characters trying to figure out  how to harness the powers offered by the  darkness  called stasis in order to fight it but  the most pressing threat  is aramis a member of the alien race  known as the fallen  who has gotten hold of stasis and is  raising an army to wield it  taking her out is your goal for the  first few hours of the expansion  but that's mostly a vehicle to getting  stasis into your hands  so you can run wild with it  stasis is the real star of beyond light  offering a new brand of abilities that  require you to rethink your strategies  the powers of stasis debuff enemies  slowing them down  freezing them solid or walling them off  behind giant ice crystals  where most abilities and supers in  destiny 2 are dedicated to damaging  enemies or healing teammates  stasis adds capabilities for controlling  the battlefield  changing the landscape and altering the  odds these powers are a nice refresher  for guardian capabilities  and feel significantly different from  everything else already available  the icy approach of stasis requires you  to figure out how to best use it against  enemies  and how to best avoid getting frozen by  opponents as stasis becomes a more  regular part of destiny 2  it's easy to imagine ways it can be  paired with existing abilities and  weapons  to pave the way for a whole new set of  tactics stasis also comes with a bunch  of customizations you can earn as you  play  amping up the effectiveness of some  elements of your new capabilities while  exacting tolls like drops and character  stats  destiny 2 has come a long way in  providing ways to spec out your  characters  and stasis deepens that system with  additional satisfying choices  however a lot of beyond light is destiny  as usual  the quest to get your new stasis powers  for instance often consists of the usual  shoot x number of y enemy grind there  also continues to be a heavy reliance on  bounties which require completing  minor objectives that are mostly about  racking up kills with specific weapons  or abilities  and which can be boring to slog through  especially when it slows you down from  accessing cool new stasis elements  but while some of the gameplay can be  predictable europa is an impressive new  offering  it's a big location with varied  environments to explore  including frozen wastes ravaged ruins a  fallen city  and huge sci-fi facilities the  destination also adds dynamic weather to  destiny 2 for the first time  and while it's not a drastic change a  blizzard whipping up in the middle of a  firefight to kill visibility  forces you to change how you play just  enough to make europa  dangerous and unstable bungie has also  gone  much further in developing the story you  uncover along the way through the  expansion  the battle against airmass is mixed up  with varrix an old destiny 1 character  and deals with their disagreement on how  best to serve and protect the scattered  fallen race  it was never meant to be an empire  it was meant to be home  finding and harnessing stasis expands  the story of the exo stranger  another destiny 1 character and finally  sheds light on a bunch of questions that  have lingered since the confusing  destiny one campaign  i once asked guardians to destroy the  black heart  to prevent darkness's arrival  success may have been achieved but i now  know that fake comes knocking sooner or  later  this expansion tells a coherent story  that's grounded in interactions between  characters you've spent lots of time  with over the years  you don't have to have read a ton of  lore to understand what's going on in  beyond light but the storytelling will  make you want to do so and reward you  with additional nuance for the  investment  we've also seen a little bit of new  content for the ongoing season of the  hunt  which centers on aldrin saav they call  me  the crow my  boss wants to see you he's the guy  players hunted down to exact revenge on  for the murder of k-6 in the forsaken  expansion  aldrin has been revived as a guardian  losing the memories of his past life and  misdeeds in the process  this season he sends you on brief but  engaging boss hunts  to earn specific perk and stat rules on  new gear while this season  like others will mostly consist of  replaying the same activities to chase  various guns and armor  the simmering conflict of working  closely with a guy your character  executed makes the season of the hunt  feel like it's burgeoning with  possibilities  the character implications of the season  already provide as big a draw to that  content as the endless loot chase  even after six years though there are  still growing pains with beyond light  and destiny 2 at large bungie has  removed a lot of content from destiny 2  with this expansion  several destinations and activities have  been vaulted with a possibility that  they  could be re-released sometime in the  future europa is a big place  but it's true that there's altogether  less of destiny 2 than there was a year  ago  that's not necessarily all bad the game  was getting unwieldy  big chunks of it were barely visited by  players and just because you could  unlock and use hundreds of guns  didn't mean they were all worth the  effort but for a game that is both  built on and hampered by repetition less  content means less variety and that  means things can get stale  all the quicker but this is also the  most alive destiny 2  has felt at least since the best days of  the forsaken expansion  and maybe ever this is the closest we've  ever been to its story characters and  lore  and the most we've ever seen characters  interacting with each other in  meaningful ways  already we've uncovered a bunch of deep  cut fascinating story beats about  characters who have persisted in destiny  since the beginning  and the deep stone crypt raid is an  exciting intense and inventive challenge  and completing it altered europa in some  significant ways  beyond light might not be the biggest  destiny expansion but it does feel like  we've entered a new chapter in the  game's life  with new priorities and an approach that  makes the game more resonant beyond  satisfying shooting  on the whole destiny 2 may be more same  than it is different  but what's the same like it's phenomenal  raids and tight satisfying gameplay  is still pretty great and what's  different is making the game all the  more worthwhile  you
 

